app mcp-server-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "Design contract for `orb mcp [--program <file>]`, the MCP server as a std program over stdio. Words reach it as the hook cli-mcp ({ argv, cwd }; `orb mcp install` stays cli-mcp-install). Newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0: MCP_LINE_IN { line } is one stdin line, answered by MCP_LINE_OUT { line } (one compact JSON reply line) or by nothing. The cases: (1) a blank line is skipped, no reply; (2) text that is not JSON is the reply with id null and error -32700, message `parse error: invalid JSON` (the Rust server's serde detail is not reproduced: the contract pins the code -32700 and the null id only); (3) a message with no id (a notification, e.g. notifications/initialized) gets no reply; (4) `initialize` answers protocolVersion = the asked one when it is 2025-06-18, 2025-03-26 or 2024-11-05, else 2025-06-18; capabilities { tools, prompts } and serverInfo name `orb` and version = what `orb --version` answers (`orb X.Y.Z`; anything else refuses to start with status 500); (5) `ping` answers result {}; (6) an unknown method answers error -32601 `method not found: <method>`; (7) `prompts/list` lists the one prompt `build` with the optional argument `app`; `prompts/get` of any other name answers -32602 `unknown prompt <name>`; (8) `tools/list` carries the language tools validate, complete, format, operators, patterns, behaviors, describe_behavior, read_behavior, play, test, reference, evaluate, each with an inputSchema of type object, then one tool per hook the hosted program declares (name, description from the hook's event, inputSchema { body required, headers }); a hook named like a language tool refuses the program at boot; (9) `tools/call` of an unknown tool is a tool result with isError true and text `orb has no tool <name>`, never a protocol error; a missing required argument is isError true naming it; a success is { content: [{ type text, text }], structuredContent, isError false }, a non-object value wrapped as { value }; (10) `tools/call` of a hook tool delivers the arguments' body (JSON as its text, a string as it is) with headers (content-type application/json default, names lower-cased) as the hook's request and answers { status, body } with the body parsed when it is JSON, else text; (11) a language tool runs only once the installed language answers; a failed setup is the tool's isError text `the language is not set up: <detail>`, retried on the next call. Reply keys are compact JSON in alphabetical order (key order is not significant to a client; the goldens pin it). Language tools map to behavior/* and program/* operators (validate: program/validate, format: program/print, behaviors: behavior/catalog, describe_behavior: behavior/describe, read_behavior: behavior/source, play: program/step); hook tools to program/inputs and program/dispatch. Evaluate wraps the expression in a one-transition program built with quasiquote, plays it through program/step with the request entity and payload, and answers the value the transition emits (checked against `orb evaluate`: [+,2,3] is 5, [>,@payload.amount,@entity.total] with total 3 and amount 4 is true). Reference and test have no port yet. The server composes std-stdio-lines for byte-safe UTF-8 line framing and output; it acknowledges each request only after answering, and ends after EOF and all queued requests are answered."
]

type McpJson = string | number | boolean | [McpJson] | Map string McpJson

orbital McpServerSpec {
  expects entity McpSession [runtime] {
    id : string!
    program : string!
    pending : string!
  }
  expects trait McpServer {
    state serving
    emits {
      MCP_LINE_OUT { line : string! }
    }
  }
  expects page stdio -> McpServer
}
